novadeck: report landscape physical size on the composite-rotation path.

Companion to 0001 (composite rotation, upstream PR #2228). That patch transposes
the LOGICAL output to landscape when g_bRotated (portrait-native panel, 90/270),
but wlserver_set_output_info() is still handed the connector's raw PORTRAIT
mmWidth/mmHeight. The result is an incoherent wl_output: a landscape 2560x1440
mode advertised over a portrait 78x140mm physical size, so any client deriving DPI
(SteamUI's automatic UI scale) gets a wrong, asymmetric value and mis-scales.

The EDID channel that WOULD carry the swapped dims (WritePatchedEdid(.., g_bRotated))
is a no-op here: internal DSI panels ship no EDID, and PatchEdid() bails on empty
input. So wl_output geometry is the only physical size Steam sees, and it must be
swapped to stay coherent with the rotated resolution.

Swap phys_width/phys_height when g_bRotated, matching the transpose the resolution
and (where present) the EDID already apply. Manual swap to mirror the existing
g_bRotated tmp-swap in drm_set_refresh (no new header dependency).

Applies -p1 on top of 0001 with line-offset fuzz (anchors verified).

diff --git a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
--- a/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
+++ b/src/Backends/DRMBackend.cpp
@@ -1138,10 +1138,20 @@ static bool setup_best_connector(struct drm_t *drm, bool force, bool initial)
 	// Don't allow rollback of mode_id after connector change
 	drm->current.mode_id = drm->pending.mode_id;

+	// The composite-rotation path (g_bRotated) transposes the LOGICAL output to
+	// landscape, but the connector reports the panel's PORTRAIT mmWidth/mmHeight.
+	// Internal DSI panels have no EDID for WritePatchedEdid() to swap, so wl_output
+	// geometry is the only physical size Steam sees; swap it too or DPI (and SteamUI's
+	// automatic UI scale) is derived from a portrait size over a landscape resolution.
+	int nPhysWidth  = (int) best->GetModeConnector()->mmWidth;
+	int nPhysHeight = (int) best->GetModeConnector()->mmHeight;
+	if ( g_bRotated ) {
+		int nTmp = nPhysWidth; nPhysWidth = nPhysHeight; nPhysHeight = nTmp;
+	}
 	const struct wlserver_output_info wlserver_output_info = {
 		.description = description,
-		.phys_width = (int) best->GetModeConnector()->mmWidth,
-		.phys_height = (int) best->GetModeConnector()->mmHeight,
+		.phys_width = nPhysWidth,
+		.phys_height = nPhysHeight,
 	};
 	wlserver_lock();
 	wlserver_set_output_info(&wlserver_output_info);
